WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
Think about this: Which service
description is appropriate?

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:04.980
Let’s work through it together.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.900
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 3: Define a
service that creates real value.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.980
Useful support can include organizing
records a client supplies, tracking

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.860
missing information, explaining the source
of a status update, and

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.760
coordinating a professional review.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.600
That value depends on accurate work and
permitted activities.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.300
Locating a possible fund does not
automatically authorize you to represent a

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.960
claimant, charge a fee, purchase rights,
or file papers.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.340
Write a one-page service description: what
you do, what you do not decide,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.920
what you charge only if permitted and
agreed, and when you refer the matter.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.300
Explain that an owner may have a direct
claim route.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.760
Show any prospective client where the
official process is described, without

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.440
suggesting that your business is the
government or that payment to you is

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.340
mandatory. Business income is uncertain.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.560
Training, tools, legal review, and time
are costs.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.240
Avoid advertising a typical recovery or
monthly income unless you have a

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.180
sound basis for the specific claim.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.040
This course teaches a process, not an
income promise.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.200
Pause and try this.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:19.440
Draft a plain-language service description
with a direct-claim disclosure

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.320
and a professional-referral boundary.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.400
Use no income claims.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.720
Quick knowledge check. Which service
description is appropriate?

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.460
The answer: We organize authorized records
and coordinate permitted

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.340
assistance; outcomes require verification.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.340
Describe the actual work and its limits
rather than claiming control over a

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:44.240
government disbursement. Keep the source,
the date, and the unknowns

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.600
visible. I'll see you in the next lesson.
